<script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://nbasalaries.com/teams/golden-state-warriors/#faq","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://nbasalaries.com/teams/golden-state-warriors/"},"mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Who is the highest-paid player on the Golden State Warriors?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Stephen Curry has the largest current cap hit at $62,587,158. His listed cash salary is $62,587,158."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the Golden State Warriors payroll?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The active roster cap payroll is $220,838,432 for 2026–27 in the 2026-10-21 snapshot. Dead cap and cap holds are separate."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much of the salary cap does the roster use?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Standard-roster cap charges equal 133.87% of the NBA’s $164,961,000 salary cap. This can exceed 100% because NBA rules allow certain exceptions."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are future contract totals fully guaranteed?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Scheduled years can include player options, team options and conditional protection. The contract table identifies options where confirmed."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why are salary and cap hit different?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Incentives, contract rules and minimum-salary adjustments can make a player’s cash pay differ from the amount charged to the team’s salary cap."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How Has the Warriors’ Payroll Changed Over Time?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Track Golden State Warriors payroll in dollars and as a share of the league’s salary cap. Comparing cap share helps put different seasons on the same scale. Swipe Left or Right to Explore Seasons Tap the Graph for Details Tap or hover a season for its details. Past seasons use historical cap payroll; 2026–27 is the current active roster plus dead cap. Future transactions can change the current-season figure."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which Pacific Team Spends the Most?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Explore the other Pacific Division teams and compare the contracts behind their payrolls."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What Does the Golden State Warriors’ Payroll Look Like in 2026-27?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Golden State Warriors salaries across 15 standard contracts add up to $220.84 million in projected cap payroll for 2026–27. Curry leads at $62.59 million, followed by Butler at $56.83 million and Green at $27.68 million. Together they take roughly 66.6% of that total. That leaves around a third of the payroll for the other twelve standard contracts. Porzingis is the next-largest commitment at $20 million, while Moody’s salary reaches $12.5 million. The Warriors are concentrating most of their spending on the veterans around Curry, with smaller deals filling out the rotation. The Golden State Warriors standard roster accounts for $220.84M. Add $0.00M in dead cap to reach $220.84M before cap holds. Holds are separate accounting charges, not signed salary payments."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What does going over the tax line mean?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The luxury tax is an additional team expense. It rises in bands as tax salary moves above the threshold; teams with a recent history of paying tax can face higher repeater rates. The final bill depends on the season-end calculation."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which Eras Cost the Warriors the Most?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The Warriors began in Philadelphia in 1946. Golden State won championships in 2015, 2017, 2018 and 2022."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which Warriors Contracts Expire Next?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Butler and Green are both under contract through 2026–27, so Golden State faces big decisions next summer. Curry signed a two-year extension worth about $116 million in September that runs through 2028–29, with a player option in the final year, and Brandin Podziemski’s five-year, $110.00 million extension, agreed in October, runs to 2031–32. Porzingis, Horford and Melton hold player options for 2027–28. Scheduled cap payroll for 2027–28 stands at $135.55 million, including options and non-guaranteed amounts, with Curry’s $55.70 million the largest piece. That gives the next round of signings a major role in shaping the Warriors’ future spending."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How Does the Golden State Warriors’ Payroll Compare With the Rest of the NBA?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Golden State Warriors rank #2 of 30 by 2026–27 cap payroll. Each bar is drawn to scale, and the change compares with the same measure for 2025–26."}}]}</script>
